WEBVTT

00:13.875 --> 00:14.957
[dramatic music playing]

00:14.958 --> 00:15.875
[Katara] Water.

00:22.916 --> 00:23.958
[Katara] Earth.

00:31.083 --> 00:31.916
[Katara] Fire.

00:38.875 --> 00:39.750
[Katara] Air.

00:48.833 --> 00:52.791
[Katara] Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

00:54.375 --> 00:57.332
Then everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

00:57.333 --> 00:59.583
[tense music playing]

01:00.875 --> 01:02.375
[Katara] Only the Avatar,

01:04.000 --> 01:07.041
master of all four elements,
could stop them.

01:10.166 --> 01:12.624
But when the world needed him most,

01:12.625 --> 01:14.000
he vanished.

01:15.083 --> 01:16.540
A hundred years passed,

01:16.541 --> 01:18.958
and my brother and I discovered
the new Avatar,

01:19.458 --> 01:20.916
an Airbender named Aang.

01:21.625 --> 01:24.207
Since we saved the Northern Water Tribe,

01:24.208 --> 01:26.875
Aang has learned to be
a pretty good Waterbender.

01:28.041 --> 01:30.500
That leaves two more elements to master,

01:31.291 --> 01:32.166
earth

01:32.833 --> 01:34.208
and fire.

01:35.958 --> 01:39.832
But as the Fire Nation conquers
more and more of the world,

01:39.833 --> 01:41.916
we're running out of time to stop them.

01:42.666 --> 01:44.750
Even though he has more to learn,

01:45.333 --> 01:49.332
we believe Aang can save the world.

01:49.333 --> 01:51.708
[dramatic music playing]

01:54.916 --> 01:56.332
[tense music playing]

01:56.333 --> 01:58.333
[people clamoring]

02:01.750 --> 02:02.583
[grunts]

02:08.208 --> 02:10.124
- [groans]
- Come on. We have to keep going.

02:10.125 --> 02:11.458
There's no point.

02:12.125 --> 02:14.290
Okay, I know you're hurting,

02:14.291 --> 02:15.958
but we need to keep going.

02:17.041 --> 02:20.249
That way, soldiers moving fast.

02:20.250 --> 02:23.624
This way, Kyoshi Warriors
coming to get us out of here.

02:23.625 --> 02:25.666
No one is coming to save us.

02:27.125 --> 02:28.625
Why did we run?

02:30.041 --> 02:31.541
It would've been faster to burn.

02:33.916 --> 02:36.583
No one is coming.

02:41.416 --> 02:42.625
Then we save ourselves.

02:43.916 --> 02:46.707
If they kill me, I will not die easy.

02:46.708 --> 02:50.041
I will die on my feet, fighting,
and so will you.

03:00.000 --> 03:01.249
- [swooshing]
- [woman gasps]

03:01.250 --> 03:02.707
[man grunts]

03:02.708 --> 03:04.708
[people clamoring]

03:06.166 --> 03:08.583
[tense music continues]

03:19.041 --> 03:20.332
[growling in distance]

03:20.333 --> 03:22.333
[mysterious music playing]

03:24.916 --> 03:26.499
[Appa grunts]

03:26.500 --> 03:27.333
[Aang] Yah!

03:32.250 --> 03:34.250
[dramatic music playing]

03:48.708 --> 03:50.708
[adventurous music playing]

03:54.583 --> 03:55.500
[grunts]

03:56.000 --> 03:57.790
[groans]

03:57.791 --> 03:59.791
[quirky music playing]

04:05.083 --> 04:06.625
[screams]

04:07.791 --> 04:09.165
[grunts]

04:09.166 --> 04:10.249
[groans]

04:10.250 --> 04:12.458
[triumphant music playing]

04:16.000 --> 04:18.165
[action music playing]

04:18.166 --> 04:19.291
[soldiers grunt]

04:22.666 --> 04:25.040
[Sai] Time to go. Okay. Okay.

04:25.041 --> 04:26.124
[soldier yells]

04:26.125 --> 04:28.291
[grunting]

04:38.708 --> 04:39.541
[soldier 2] Aah!

04:40.125 --> 04:42.916
[grunting]

04:45.750 --> 04:47.166
[solider 3 yells]

04:48.333 --> 04:49.707
[solider 4 yells]

04:49.708 --> 04:51.000
[soldiers yelling]

04:57.541 --> 04:58.750
[solider grunts]

05:00.833 --> 05:02.166
[grunting]

05:23.041 --> 05:24.000
[soldier 5] There he is!

05:24.875 --> 05:26.000
Get him!

05:29.958 --> 05:32.208
[people clamoring]

05:37.125 --> 05:38.290
[Sokka] Hey, flame head!

05:38.291 --> 05:39.666
[grunting]

05:53.208 --> 05:54.457
[solider 6] Huh?

05:54.458 --> 05:55.791
[grunting]

06:04.166 --> 06:05.000
[chuckles softly]

06:06.666 --> 06:08.124
[music fades]

06:08.125 --> 06:09.250
Lose something?

06:10.041 --> 06:11.083
[soldier grunts]

06:11.583 --> 06:13.791
Yeah, I lost track of my many victories.

06:14.291 --> 06:15.250
[both chuckle]

06:17.916 --> 06:19.624
[Suki chuckles]

06:19.625 --> 06:21.625
[sentimental music playing]

06:35.125 --> 06:37.125
[music fades]

06:38.166 --> 06:39.208
[man grunts]

06:42.416 --> 06:43.916
[Katara] Do you wanna help me heal him?

06:47.291 --> 06:48.958
You'll have to learn it eventually.

06:55.083 --> 06:56.166
[man shudders]

07:13.083 --> 07:15.666
[gasps] I don't believe it.

07:16.791 --> 07:18.291
Get lots of rest, okay?

07:19.458 --> 07:21.416
Not until this war is over.

07:24.375 --> 07:26.625
[uplifting music playing]

07:45.541 --> 07:47.374
It really has been a long time.

07:47.375 --> 07:48.749
[Suki] It sure has.

07:48.750 --> 07:50.750
You shot up
like a bamboo sprout. [chuckles]

07:51.500 --> 07:53.000
- Are you…
- [Aang] Am I…

07:55.208 --> 07:56.665
[Suki] No. [chuckles]

07:56.666 --> 07:57.915
- Hey.
- [Sokka] Hmm?

07:57.916 --> 07:59.125
Nice job out there.

08:03.666 --> 08:04.583
[chuckles]

08:05.291 --> 08:06.291
[chuckling]

08:11.750 --> 08:13.958
I can't tell you what it means to see you.

08:17.166 --> 08:18.415
All of you.

08:18.416 --> 08:20.583
What are you doing back
in the Earth Kingdom?

08:21.083 --> 08:22.958
I'm gonna rescue my earthbending teacher.

08:24.125 --> 08:27.125
- Do you know where they're holding Bumi?
- [Sai] Uh, yes.

08:27.708 --> 08:30.583
He's locked in a metal tower.
Back in Omashu.

08:31.083 --> 08:32.749
He can't bend his way out of it.

08:32.750 --> 08:35.583
I don't care.
I need to learn earthbending.

08:36.291 --> 08:37.832
And I'm gonna get my friend.

08:37.833 --> 08:39.333
[tense chord plays]

08:40.291 --> 08:42.458
[dramatic music playing]

08:56.583 --> 08:59.499
[wind howling]

08:59.500 --> 09:01.500
[mysterious music playing]

09:26.833 --> 09:27.749
[guard] Hey!

09:27.750 --> 09:28.625
[guard 2] Halt!

09:29.708 --> 09:31.958
I bet one of you guys has a key for this,
don't you?

09:33.500 --> 09:34.916
- [grunts]
- [grunts]

09:38.958 --> 09:39.791
[guard 2 grunts]

09:50.250 --> 09:51.208
Aang!

09:52.041 --> 09:53.208
You shouldn't be here.

09:54.083 --> 09:55.374
Bumi, there you are.

09:55.375 --> 09:58.958
You usually wait a century between visits.
This is… this is much too soon.

09:59.666 --> 10:02.290
The years are catching up with you. Hmm.

10:02.291 --> 10:05.875
Many things are catching up with you,
I imagine. Stars, planets, and the like.

10:06.500 --> 10:08.374
Okay. Let's go.

10:08.375 --> 10:10.957
You'll teach me earthbending.
Then we'll fight the Fire Lord.

10:10.958 --> 10:12.207
No!

10:12.208 --> 10:15.333
[chuckles] No! I'm far too busy.

10:15.916 --> 10:18.040
Bumi, this is… It's no time for jokes.

10:18.041 --> 10:20.832
That's right.
This is the time that you leave.

10:20.833 --> 10:21.999
Immediately.

10:22.000 --> 10:24.665
You wanna stay… here?

10:24.666 --> 10:26.708
That's why I surrendered.

10:27.750 --> 10:28.791
You what?

10:29.375 --> 10:31.415
When I left, you were in the fight.

10:31.416 --> 10:34.749
Now Omashu is in ruins,
and your people are refugees.

10:34.750 --> 10:36.583
What did you do?

10:37.166 --> 10:38.416
Nothing!

10:39.000 --> 10:40.415
I did nothing.

10:40.416 --> 10:44.875
And it was the hardest thing
I have ever done.

10:46.875 --> 10:48.290
I could've taken up arms,

10:48.291 --> 10:52.125
and my people would have followed
and died for it.

10:52.708 --> 10:56.833
To save them, I did nothing.

10:57.833 --> 10:58.832
[inhales sharply]

10:58.833 --> 11:00.166
Do you see?

11:01.166 --> 11:05.374
I had to feel everything

11:05.375 --> 11:08.624
so that I could feel nothing,

11:08.625 --> 11:13.333
which is the key to feeling everything.

11:15.500 --> 11:19.166
What do you know of jing, hmm?

11:21.041 --> 11:23.707
The monks said
it's the energy used to fight.

11:23.708 --> 11:26.457
Positive jing when you attack.
And negative jing when you retreat.

11:26.458 --> 11:30.541
- Which we should be doing right now.
- What about neutral jing?

11:32.166 --> 11:33.749
There are three kinds of jing?

11:33.750 --> 11:36.499
There are 85 different kinds of jing.

11:36.500 --> 11:39.124
Momo knows all of them. Hello.

11:39.125 --> 11:40.833
[squeaks]

11:41.791 --> 11:44.457
[Bumi] People use jing every day,
and they aren't aware of it,

11:44.458 --> 11:49.165
but you must become aware of it, Aang.

11:49.166 --> 11:52.249
You must master neutral jing

11:52.250 --> 11:55.125
to learn earthbending.

11:55.708 --> 11:57.583
Master neutral jing?

11:58.250 --> 11:59.915
- Master doing nothing?
- [Bumi chuckles]

11:59.916 --> 12:01.499
It may look that way,

12:01.500 --> 12:04.540
but it is waiting and listening

12:04.541 --> 12:06.250
for the right time

12:06.958 --> 12:08.083
to strike.

12:09.083 --> 12:12.708
But… but this… this is the moment.

12:13.333 --> 12:16.999
You come with me,
and we can defeat the Fire Lord together.

12:17.000 --> 12:18.166
Please, Bumi.

12:18.875 --> 12:20.500
You're my oldest friend. Just…

12:23.083 --> 12:24.041
just…

12:25.583 --> 12:26.791
just be my teacher.

12:27.375 --> 12:30.291
Your teacher will be
a master of neutral jing.

12:31.958 --> 12:35.000
A teacher who waits and listens.

12:36.333 --> 12:39.958
Maybe it will be a new friend.

12:41.791 --> 12:43.333
You should go, Aang.

12:44.500 --> 12:46.708
The guards
will be changing their shifts soon.

12:47.708 --> 12:50.208
If they find you,
all the time in the world

12:50.791 --> 12:55.250
will suddenly become no time at all.

12:55.750 --> 12:56.583
[sighs]

12:57.166 --> 12:59.833
I'll see you another time, my friend.

13:00.583 --> 13:02.583
[somber music playing]

13:08.625 --> 13:10.457
[guard groans]

13:10.458 --> 13:11.416
[guard 2] What happened?

13:13.583 --> 13:14.874
[Bumi] Mmm.

13:14.875 --> 13:16.707
Mmm. Huh.

13:16.708 --> 13:18.208
Is it time for tea?

13:20.000 --> 13:21.040
[rain pattering]

13:21.041 --> 13:23.041
[hogaku music playing]

13:23.833 --> 13:25.665
[inhales]

13:25.666 --> 13:26.916
[exhales]

13:37.875 --> 13:39.250
Thank you.

13:39.750 --> 13:42.374
- Doesn't the rain feel glorious?
- Mm-hmm.

13:42.375 --> 13:43.291
[sighs]

13:50.875 --> 13:52.665
You need to move faster, Uncle.

13:52.666 --> 13:55.790
Ah, but if I rush,
I'll miss the waft of rind on the breeze,

13:55.791 --> 13:59.291
the silky mud
settling into the grooves of my skin.

14:00.583 --> 14:03.958
Every time you help someone else,
your own bag gets emptier.

14:04.750 --> 14:06.958
[Iroh] That's a terrible way
to look at the world.

14:08.166 --> 14:10.541
The world is terrible.

14:11.291 --> 14:14.249
This… this place is terrible.

14:14.250 --> 14:16.375
Melon yams are terrible.

14:17.500 --> 14:18.625
[sighs]

14:19.958 --> 14:22.458
You know, we started out
picking melon yams.

14:23.166 --> 14:25.540
Then it was kale and tomatoes.

14:25.541 --> 14:27.707
Then mung beans
and pepper plums and cabbages.

14:27.708 --> 14:31.625
And now we're back to melon yams.

14:34.500 --> 14:36.458
How long can we do this?

14:37.125 --> 14:39.541
Hiding out like fugitives.

14:40.125 --> 14:40.958
[sighs]

14:42.791 --> 14:45.083
We are fugitives.

14:54.250 --> 14:56.250
[dramatic, sinister music playing]

15:04.041 --> 15:05.207
[music fades]

15:05.208 --> 15:07.165
[indistinct chatter]

15:07.166 --> 15:08.541
What are you gonna say?

15:09.291 --> 15:12.457
The truth because he already knows.

15:12.458 --> 15:15.166
The truth is open to interpretation.

15:22.708 --> 15:26.582
General Li, what is the status
of our holdings in the Earth Kingdom?

15:26.583 --> 15:29.749
After Princess Azula's brilliant conquest

15:29.750 --> 15:31.457
in the city of New Ozai,

15:31.458 --> 15:33.749
certain skirmishes continue.

15:33.750 --> 15:34.958
Skirmishes?

15:36.666 --> 15:39.999
Losses, my exalted Fire Lord.

15:40.000 --> 15:41.332
Pretty language.

15:41.333 --> 15:44.582
Pretty enough for last words.

15:44.583 --> 15:47.833
General, you are relieved of your command.

15:48.333 --> 15:50.624
As are you, Admiral Kaga.

15:50.625 --> 15:53.583
And that is not open to interpretation.

15:55.416 --> 15:57.375
We stand relieved.

16:06.250 --> 16:11.165
Make room underground
for two new prison guards. [giggles]

16:11.166 --> 16:12.290
[Ozai] Princess Azula,

16:12.291 --> 16:15.916
the family has always been blessed
by the wisdom of its second children.

16:16.750 --> 16:18.250
The floor is yours.

16:19.166 --> 16:23.040
While the general has waged
a slow and ponderous campaign

16:23.041 --> 16:25.707
bogged down
in the wilds of the Earth Kingdom…

16:25.708 --> 16:27.832
Land war in Earth Kingdom.

16:27.833 --> 16:29.624
Classic blunder.

16:29.625 --> 16:32.790
…my forces have used
the imprisoned Earthbenders

16:32.791 --> 16:35.166
to make swift progress to the territory.

16:35.833 --> 16:39.499
Soon, we will be in a position

16:39.500 --> 16:44.291
to move heavy artillery
directly from our ships at sea over land

16:44.791 --> 16:46.166
to their very doorstep.

16:46.750 --> 16:49.332
The decision to put you in charge
of the Omashu campaign

16:49.333 --> 16:51.375
continues to yield dividends.

16:52.916 --> 16:57.666
Next… we take the Earth Kingdom
by ripping out its heart.

16:58.250 --> 17:00.624
The so-called impenetrable city.

17:00.625 --> 17:02.540
The unwieldy metropolis.

17:02.541 --> 17:05.875
The seat of earthbending power.

17:06.875 --> 17:08.583
Ba Sing Se

17:09.625 --> 17:10.540
will fall.

17:10.541 --> 17:12.582
Even the Dragon of the West failed.

17:12.583 --> 17:14.749
Does no one read history anymore?

17:14.750 --> 17:19.083
Our last siege of Ba Sing Se
was a colossal failure.

17:19.708 --> 17:23.249
Doomed from its planning
and abandoned in its execution

17:23.250 --> 17:25.708
by the traitor General Iroh.

17:26.666 --> 17:29.458
And how will you do
what has never been done?

17:31.333 --> 17:33.458
By using what I learned from you

17:34.541 --> 17:35.875
and enhancing it.

17:38.166 --> 17:42.957
We amass an overwhelming force
outside the walls,

17:42.958 --> 17:46.707
drawing attention
through drill tanks and war balloons.

17:46.708 --> 17:49.083
Then we strike from beneath.

17:50.000 --> 17:52.582
My earthbending prisoners will tunnel
under the walls,

17:52.583 --> 17:56.665
and our troops will ravage the city
from the inside out.

17:56.666 --> 17:58.458
They will never see it coming.

18:00.333 --> 18:04.041
There are but three people in the world

18:04.625 --> 18:06.833
who have the power
to determine its future.

18:07.333 --> 18:09.833
You, my Fire Lord,

18:10.583 --> 18:11.625
the Avatar,

18:12.583 --> 18:13.791
and the Earth King.

18:14.375 --> 18:19.000
This will neutralize the Earth King.
And your power can only grow.

18:19.625 --> 18:21.500
I await only your consent to begin.

18:24.958 --> 18:28.125
It is as solid a strategy
as I myself could've planned…

18:31.000 --> 18:32.333
at your age.

18:34.333 --> 18:35.500
It is approved.

18:37.083 --> 18:40.208
Under the direction of a talented,

18:40.750 --> 18:42.999
decorated prodigy

18:43.000 --> 18:46.291
of the agile younger generation.

18:50.625 --> 18:51.958
General Tran!

18:58.750 --> 19:00.041
Thank you, Fire Lord Ozai.

19:00.750 --> 19:05.083
I will do my utmost to repay the trust
you have bestowed upon me tenfold.

19:06.250 --> 19:07.666
To the Flame Eternal.

19:08.375 --> 19:09.666
Dismissed!

19:12.416 --> 19:14.416
[indistinct chatter]

19:18.041 --> 19:19.041
[Ozai] Azula.

19:20.666 --> 19:21.500
[doors close]

19:22.125 --> 19:24.915
You have feelings about my decision

19:24.916 --> 19:27.875
to put General Tran
in charge of your mission.

19:29.250 --> 19:31.750
Speak… freely.

19:33.125 --> 19:35.208
Of course I trust your judgment.

19:36.208 --> 19:39.458
You truly are blessed
with the blood of your ancestors.

19:40.291 --> 19:42.833
You wanna fight, to conquer.

19:43.500 --> 19:45.708
But for you, I have a special mission.

19:46.916 --> 19:49.790
Well, Father, you gave Ba Sing Se to Tran.

19:49.791 --> 19:52.749
And I can't conquer Omashu twice,
so what is it you desire?

19:52.750 --> 19:55.000
Your brother, Zuko.

19:56.833 --> 19:58.250
Zuko is dead.

20:00.708 --> 20:02.000
He died in the North

20:02.666 --> 20:06.666
after turning traitor
and attacking Admiral Zhao.

20:08.583 --> 20:12.082
Even if he were alive, you yourself
declared him a war criminal.

20:12.083 --> 20:14.333
And I have decided to pardon him.

20:15.166 --> 20:16.958
Zuko is alive

20:17.666 --> 20:20.625
and hiding out in a far-flung corner
of the Earth Kingdom.

20:22.583 --> 20:24.375
I want you to retrieve him.

20:26.750 --> 20:28.083
Retrieve him.

20:29.791 --> 20:30.707
And do what?

20:30.708 --> 20:32.291
Bring him home.

20:34.125 --> 20:36.791
It's time to get our family in order.

20:37.875 --> 20:39.875
[foreboding music playing]

20:47.000 --> 20:49.166
I serve at the pleasure of the Fire Lord.

20:57.375 --> 20:58.500
Princess Azula.

20:59.000 --> 20:59.958
What?

21:00.875 --> 21:03.874
I know this must be strange,
but it was a surprise to me as well.

21:03.875 --> 21:06.083
- I am deeply unworthy--
- That's right.

21:06.583 --> 21:08.208
You are unworthy.

21:10.291 --> 21:13.540
Your plan is perfect.
I will devote myself to it.

21:13.541 --> 21:17.166
Flattery is the mud
in which politicians wallow.

21:17.791 --> 21:19.832
I thought you were a soldier.

21:19.833 --> 21:23.166
Only in the foulest mud
can the perfect crimson lotus grow.

21:25.041 --> 21:26.083
Crimson?

21:27.458 --> 21:28.416
Yes.

21:29.916 --> 21:31.250
With the blood of your enemies.

21:32.333 --> 21:34.249
Do you know what they are calling you?

21:34.250 --> 21:36.582
I don't pay attention to court gossip.

21:36.583 --> 21:38.375
The Bane of Omashu.

21:40.750 --> 21:42.332
Well, it's no Dragon of the West.

21:42.333 --> 21:43.500
[Tran] Please understand me.

21:44.000 --> 21:46.874
Whatever victories we achieve
will be in your name.

21:46.875 --> 21:49.915
Every conquest will serve to glorify you.

21:49.916 --> 21:52.875
Don't you mean glorify the Fire Lord?

21:54.125 --> 21:55.375
As I said,

21:55.958 --> 21:57.583
every victory in your name.

21:58.958 --> 22:01.250
Every win to glorify…

22:04.833 --> 22:06.000
the Fire Lord.

22:10.833 --> 22:14.291
We will consider any accolades
you wish to bestow upon us.

22:16.750 --> 22:18.541
You are dismissed.

22:28.958 --> 22:31.125
[indistinct chatter]

22:40.916 --> 22:43.041
I was supposed to get four coins.

22:43.750 --> 22:45.915
Yesterday it was three. Today it's two?

22:45.916 --> 22:49.666
Four for the day, minus one for rent,
one for the broken handle.

22:50.625 --> 22:53.165
That spade was broken
when I picked it up this morning.

22:53.166 --> 22:54.999
And as for rent, I don't sleep inside.

22:55.000 --> 22:57.624
I sleep under the stars like an animal.

22:57.625 --> 23:01.583
Don't matter where you sleep.
It's all company land. Now move along.

23:18.625 --> 23:22.040
What kind of a prince
sweats all day for pennies?

23:22.041 --> 23:23.374
A wise prince.

23:23.375 --> 23:26.249
A prince who understands
the value of hard work,

23:26.250 --> 23:30.583
who respects the struggle of his people
because he has shared in those struggles.

23:31.833 --> 23:33.083
They're beneath me.

23:34.458 --> 23:36.458
This whole place is beneath me.

23:38.416 --> 23:40.416
[foreboding music playing]

23:50.791 --> 23:51.791
[man] Who's next?

23:52.625 --> 23:53.665
Here you go.

23:53.666 --> 23:55.666
[somber music playing]

23:58.625 --> 24:00.249
Yes, sit right here.

24:00.250 --> 24:02.291
[woman] I can't believe you're here.

24:03.833 --> 24:05.582
I've seen this before.

24:05.583 --> 24:07.500
Just show us the way.

24:08.000 --> 24:09.125
We need your help.

24:09.750 --> 24:11.375
What's wrong? Are you hurt?

24:12.708 --> 24:13.999
Oh, hi.

24:14.000 --> 24:16.833
No, I was just talking to the… flower.

24:17.958 --> 24:19.125
Is that weird?

24:21.208 --> 24:23.041
I've never seen anything like it.

24:23.541 --> 24:26.500
It's, uh… it's a painted lady.

24:27.291 --> 24:30.541
- [Katara] Hmm.
- I just had to say a little prayer.

24:31.041 --> 24:32.083
Look at her.

24:33.666 --> 24:37.582
When I was little, my mother told me
that these flowers would grow

24:37.583 --> 24:40.416
wherever the Painted Lady
touched the earth.

24:42.541 --> 24:44.041
Who's the Painted Lady?

24:45.166 --> 24:48.041
Oh, she's, uh, the river spirit.

24:49.750 --> 24:52.415
She appears in the rolling mists

24:52.416 --> 24:56.583
and takes the form
of a woman painted in red and gold.

24:57.458 --> 25:02.958
Outside our village, these flowers grew
like a perfumed blanket

25:03.458 --> 25:07.458
until, um, one day, they all withered.

25:08.541 --> 25:11.791
And my mom, she understood the sign.

25:12.500 --> 25:15.583
She packed us up, and then we left and…

25:16.166 --> 25:17.332
Then a week later,

25:17.333 --> 25:20.625
the Fire Nation
burned our village to the ground.

25:23.916 --> 25:26.000
And the Painted Lady warned us.

25:26.708 --> 25:32.375
And… paying attention
saved our family. [chuckles]

25:38.250 --> 25:41.416
This is the first one
that I've seen since then.

25:43.708 --> 25:45.583
When you see a painted lady,

25:46.291 --> 25:47.500
it's a blessing.

25:48.875 --> 25:49.791
A sign.

25:52.291 --> 25:54.291
It means we're going the right way…

25:56.541 --> 25:58.666
whichever way that is.

26:00.958 --> 26:02.208
Somewhere safe.

26:20.958 --> 26:22.000
[Sokka] Oh!

26:23.791 --> 26:27.125
Still doing that, huh?
Just… don't change what works.

26:27.875 --> 26:29.166
Hi, stranger.

26:31.000 --> 26:31.916
Hi.

26:33.500 --> 26:34.458
Uh…

26:35.166 --> 26:36.624
Uh, how… how are you?

26:36.625 --> 26:38.040
Uh…

26:38.041 --> 26:39.000
I'm fine.

26:41.458 --> 26:42.416
Peach pear?

26:44.541 --> 26:45.707
Oh, no, I couldn't.

26:45.708 --> 26:48.249
There's a limited amount of food
and a lot of people.

26:48.250 --> 26:50.375
It's my peach pear from my rations.

26:50.958 --> 26:52.874
Then you should eat it.

26:52.875 --> 26:55.124
You're being very rude
about my peach pear.

26:55.125 --> 26:58.957
No, I love your peach pear.
I… I'm just not hungry.

26:58.958 --> 27:01.957
You're always hungry. How many times
have you threatened to eat Momo?

27:01.958 --> 27:03.082
Well, that's just a--

27:03.083 --> 27:05.625
Really good idea. He looks delicious.

27:07.833 --> 27:08.915
- [Suki chuckles]
- I…

27:08.916 --> 27:11.416
Try it. It's lovely.

27:23.625 --> 27:24.500
Mmm.

27:25.000 --> 27:26.333
[Suki] Well? [chuckles]

27:28.041 --> 27:29.249
Really good.

27:29.250 --> 27:31.083
I told you. [chuckles]

27:32.458 --> 27:34.416
So I was thinking something.

27:35.208 --> 27:37.166
About us being together.

27:38.666 --> 27:40.874
[Sokka] Right.
Like, while we're on the road?

27:40.875 --> 27:41.791
Yeah.

27:42.416 --> 27:43.916
I was thinking,

27:44.416 --> 27:45.708
while we're together,

27:46.291 --> 27:47.833
why not just be together?

27:54.208 --> 27:55.625
[wind howls]

27:56.500 --> 27:58.958
Oh, Aang's back. I, uh… I should go.

28:01.041 --> 28:02.041
I…

28:08.250 --> 28:09.208
[exhales softly]

28:12.625 --> 28:13.540
Where's Bumi?

28:13.541 --> 28:15.540
Bumi's locked up,
and he wants to stay locked up.

28:15.541 --> 28:17.874
It doesn't matter what his people need
or what I need.

28:17.875 --> 28:18.916
- Slow down.
- [Sokka] Aang!

28:20.541 --> 28:22.290
Hey, I'm glad you're back.

28:22.291 --> 28:25.082
Sai said he had something important
to tell us when we have a sec.

28:25.083 --> 28:27.582
Sorry, guys. Aang, we need to move now.

28:27.583 --> 28:30.040
I scouted the southern shore,
and it's overrun.

28:30.041 --> 28:32.415
That was our only path
to get everyone to safety.

28:32.416 --> 28:35.625
- Fire Nation's trying to box us in.
- The entire territory is covered.

28:36.125 --> 28:39.832
If they're blocking the southern shore,
then there's only one way left to go.

28:39.833 --> 28:41.333
[suspenseful music playing]

28:48.208 --> 28:49.875
[Katara] "Abandon all hope."

28:50.375 --> 28:52.208
[Sokka] Well, that's not a good sign.

28:52.791 --> 28:55.375
If only someone could fly up there
and take it down.

28:56.250 --> 28:57.208
Yeah.

29:05.083 --> 29:06.541
[cheering and applause]

29:07.291 --> 29:08.125
Show-off.

29:08.791 --> 29:10.165
It's good for morale.

29:10.166 --> 29:13.208
Everyone, stay together.
Fire Nation's on our heels.

29:14.333 --> 29:15.208
Hey.

29:16.291 --> 29:18.000
The path winds like a snake.

29:18.583 --> 29:20.583
I bet that's why they call it
Serpent's Pass.

29:24.125 --> 29:25.750
Nothing gets by you.

29:27.541 --> 29:29.040
[tense, suspenseful music playing]

29:29.041 --> 29:30.625
[Appa grunting]

29:41.375 --> 29:43.541
[chittering]

29:44.625 --> 29:47.083
[Appa grunting]

29:55.125 --> 29:56.333
[Momo chitters]

30:07.625 --> 30:09.500
Here's something else for the to-do list.

30:10.000 --> 30:12.582
Everyone from Omashu
has got 1,001 scary stories

30:12.583 --> 30:14.749
about Zuko's sister, Azula.

30:14.750 --> 30:16.832
She's the one
who slashed and burned the city.

30:16.833 --> 30:20.040
So she's actually worse than Zuko?

30:20.041 --> 30:21.416
Is that even possible?

30:21.916 --> 30:23.958
They say she throws blue fire.

30:24.833 --> 30:26.290
Like, metaphorically?

30:26.291 --> 30:28.332
No, it's literally, like, blue flames.

30:28.333 --> 30:30.499
- Do you think blue fire's cold?
- No.

30:30.500 --> 30:32.832
It's… very hot.

30:32.833 --> 30:35.665
So hot, it went all the way
around the rainbow and started over again.

30:35.666 --> 30:38.375
Got it. Scary sister. Add it to the list.

30:39.416 --> 30:41.875
There's so much to do,
and everyone's lagging. Come on.

30:44.083 --> 30:45.624
- [Sokka] Oh!
- [Katara] Sokka!

30:45.625 --> 30:48.291
- [Aang] Keep moving. A little faster.
- [Katara] Be careful.

30:50.583 --> 30:51.416
[sighs]

30:52.583 --> 30:54.249
[girl whimpers]

30:54.250 --> 30:56.833
[waves crashing]

31:02.000 --> 31:04.207
Hey, you guys okay?

31:04.208 --> 31:06.040
We're going too fast.

31:06.041 --> 31:07.750
And it's too high.

31:08.458 --> 31:10.000
I'm just a kid.

31:13.750 --> 31:14.750
So am I.

31:15.625 --> 31:19.875
Sometimes, even Airbenders
can be scared of heights. Okay?

31:23.125 --> 31:24.041
Come on.

31:25.166 --> 31:26.416
I won't let you fall.

31:35.750 --> 31:37.416
I won't let any of you fall.

31:38.458 --> 31:40.458
[uplifting music playing]

31:56.625 --> 31:58.625
[tense chord plays]

32:02.125 --> 32:04.125
[indistinct chatter]

32:10.500 --> 32:12.290
[Sokka] How are we
supposed to get through?

32:12.291 --> 32:14.457
Aang and I are both Waterbenders, Sokka.

32:14.458 --> 32:17.333
Yeah, but we need an Earthbender
to bring the path up out of the…

32:17.833 --> 32:19.624
- Oh.
- I knew he'd get there.

32:19.625 --> 32:20.541
[Katara chuckles]

32:21.375 --> 32:24.540
Well, this looks pretty deep.
It's gonna take both of us.

32:24.541 --> 32:27.416
- You ready?
- If I'm not, we know who to blame.

32:28.208 --> 32:30.374
- [Sokka chuckles]
- Just kidding, I got this.

32:30.375 --> 32:32.500
Stop hanging out with Sokka.

32:34.875 --> 32:36.875
[dramatic music playing]

33:09.541 --> 33:11.083
- Momo.
- [Momo squeaks]

33:35.291 --> 33:36.291
[Momo chitters]

33:37.375 --> 33:38.833
[squeaking]

33:59.916 --> 34:00.750
[Sokka] Oh.

34:02.583 --> 34:04.250
- [squeaks]
- Fire Nation!

34:07.166 --> 34:09.040
[people screaming]

34:09.041 --> 34:11.915
- Can you hold it on your own?
- Yeah, go help at the back.

34:11.916 --> 34:12.750
[Suki] Let's go.

34:13.333 --> 34:14.916
Everybody, move. Come on.

34:15.666 --> 34:18.583
Like, wow, man. Look at the wonder.

34:19.083 --> 34:21.500
- Less gaping, more running.
- [Suki] They're right behind us.

34:36.125 --> 34:37.875
What are they firing at?

34:40.291 --> 34:42.291
[indistinct yelling]

34:45.375 --> 34:47.540
I think that's why they call it
the Serpent's Pass.

34:47.541 --> 34:50.165
It's fighting the Fire Nation.
I think it's on our side.

34:50.166 --> 34:52.166
[suspenseful music playing]

34:52.666 --> 34:54.375
[growling softly]

35:03.375 --> 35:04.875
I think it's on its own side.

35:06.166 --> 35:09.124
- Go help the others. I got this.
- [Suki] Come on. Come on, everyone.

35:09.125 --> 35:11.707
Better rush if you're going Avatar State
and take that thing out.

35:11.708 --> 35:13.958
Yes to the rush. No to the Avatar State.

35:16.875 --> 35:18.875
[dramatic music playing]

35:21.875 --> 35:23.375
[serpent shrieks]

35:30.208 --> 35:31.458
[shrieks]

35:32.416 --> 35:33.625
[roars]

35:48.708 --> 35:50.000
Come on, everybody.

35:50.666 --> 35:52.875
- [Suki] Quickly.
- And safely. And safely.

35:55.416 --> 35:58.499
Oh, Aang looks so tiny up there next to
that great big giant beast of the sea…

35:58.500 --> 36:00.083
Oh no! He's gonna eat him!

36:00.583 --> 36:01.707
Follow me!

36:01.708 --> 36:02.874
Wha…

36:02.875 --> 36:05.916
Sokka, come on.
Let's keep moving, everybody.

36:06.583 --> 36:08.208
[growling]

36:23.250 --> 36:26.125
[roars]

36:37.875 --> 36:39.374
[music stops]

36:39.375 --> 36:40.375
[wind whistling]

36:43.750 --> 36:47.041
[roars]

36:49.041 --> 36:51.500
[snarls]

36:52.541 --> 36:54.332
[suspenseful music playing]

36:54.333 --> 36:55.249
[shrieks]

36:55.250 --> 36:57.250
- [grunts]
- Suki!

37:06.833 --> 37:08.083
- You okay?
- Yeah.

37:10.666 --> 37:11.708
[Aang] Ah!

37:12.208 --> 37:14.958
[growls]

37:15.666 --> 37:17.207
[snarls]

37:17.208 --> 37:18.583
Get to the shore.

37:19.541 --> 37:20.791
[Sokka] Katara!

37:21.291 --> 37:22.958
There's no way that's safe!

37:26.875 --> 37:28.375
[snarls]

37:34.416 --> 37:36.833
- [roars]
- [Aang grunts]

37:39.500 --> 37:42.416
[roars]

37:45.125 --> 37:47.541
[adventurous music playing]

38:06.833 --> 38:08.666
[serpent roars]

38:20.666 --> 38:25.125
[squealing]

38:36.291 --> 38:38.375
[snarls]

38:39.291 --> 38:42.041
[groans]

38:45.791 --> 38:47.791
[somber music playing]

39:01.083 --> 39:02.583
I… I didn't mean to…

39:03.166 --> 39:04.666
I didn't mean to kill it.

39:06.208 --> 39:08.749
[serpent groans]

39:08.750 --> 39:10.291
[Katara] It's still alive.

39:11.625 --> 39:15.207
Your water. Use the water
from the Spirit Oasis to heal it.

39:15.208 --> 39:16.208
No.

39:16.916 --> 39:19.124
No, we can heal it together.

39:19.125 --> 39:20.957
I can't. I haven't--

39:20.958 --> 39:23.541
No, trust me. This is how you learn.

39:29.625 --> 39:30.625
Show me.

39:34.833 --> 39:36.333
Here, hold this with me.

39:38.250 --> 39:40.416
We bend it together in balance.

39:42.708 --> 39:43.625
[Aang] Now what?

39:44.166 --> 39:46.041
[Katara] Now we move it into the wound.

39:52.250 --> 39:53.958
Now we work with the serpent.

39:54.958 --> 39:56.541
Feel its energy.

39:57.250 --> 39:58.665
The beat of its heart.

39:58.666 --> 40:01.375
The flow of blood all through its body.

40:02.750 --> 40:05.000
Let that energy flow through you.

40:05.791 --> 40:07.083
Through the water.

40:07.875 --> 40:10.500
Into its blood. Its skin.

40:11.000 --> 40:13.249
Every broken piece of its body.

40:13.250 --> 40:15.750
[gentle, inspirational music playing]

40:16.625 --> 40:18.625
[heartbeat]

40:23.750 --> 40:25.750
[serpent grunts softly]

40:30.416 --> 40:33.333
[grunts softly]

40:41.666 --> 40:43.916
[grunting softly]

40:51.666 --> 40:53.375
And now you know how to heal.

40:55.750 --> 40:56.833
Katara,

40:57.625 --> 40:59.791
I couldn't be doing any of this
without you.

41:01.875 --> 41:05.458
I'm so lucky you're the one
who broke me out of that iceberg.

41:07.458 --> 41:10.416
Yeah, you are pretty lucky, huh?
[chuckles] Let's go.

41:29.708 --> 41:32.499
[Suki] When you and Sokka and Aang
showed up on Kyoshi Island,

41:32.500 --> 41:34.707
it opened up this whole world to me.

41:34.708 --> 41:35.791
To all of us.

41:36.708 --> 41:40.332
I didn't know it would include
steam-spewing sea beasts. [chuckles]

41:40.333 --> 41:42.499
Yeah, and neither did I. [chuckles]

41:42.500 --> 41:43.708
At first.

41:44.208 --> 41:46.750
[Suki] But it's good. Even the monsters.

41:47.250 --> 41:49.125
We've been able to help a lot of people.

41:50.250 --> 41:52.791
And we may have to take this group
all the way to Ba Sing Se.

41:53.500 --> 41:55.583
If we make it,
it really is thanks to you guys.

41:56.583 --> 41:58.833
We might not even be here
if it wasn't for you.

42:00.083 --> 42:03.875
You know, before we met you,
Sokka wanted to go home.

42:05.333 --> 42:08.458
And the way you all fought to defend us,

42:09.125 --> 42:12.000
it made me see that I wasn't dumb
for believing the Avatar.

42:12.916 --> 42:16.208
For having hope
that any one person can make a difference.

42:22.375 --> 42:23.333
All done.

42:24.416 --> 42:25.333
[Suki chuckles]

42:27.750 --> 42:29.457
You know,
if you're finished teaching Aang,

42:29.458 --> 42:31.083
we could use someone like you.

42:32.125 --> 42:33.708
Join the Kyoshi Warriors?

42:36.291 --> 42:38.375
Is that even possible?
I… I'm a Waterbender.

42:39.333 --> 42:40.541
So is Kyoshi.

42:43.166 --> 42:44.125
Just a thought.

42:45.833 --> 42:47.833
[uplifting music playing]

43:14.125 --> 43:16.707
[Sokka] Nice display of bending
back there.

43:16.708 --> 43:19.832
Really gave the group a shot of confidence
to see you deal with that

43:19.833 --> 43:21.957
serpent-dragon-eel thing.

43:21.958 --> 43:23.165
[Aang chuckles]

43:23.166 --> 43:26.165
- It gave me a shot of confidence too.
- Good.

43:26.166 --> 43:27.416
Didn't know I could heal.

43:28.291 --> 43:31.583
Hey, and I didn't mean to tell you
what to do about the Avatar State.

43:32.083 --> 43:36.124
It's just when you did it in the North,
it was so powerful, and it was so…

43:36.125 --> 43:37.375
I didn't though.

43:39.750 --> 43:41.374
I surrendered to the Ocean Spirit,

43:41.375 --> 43:44.541
and it used me to channel its power
to defeat the Fire Nation.

43:45.041 --> 43:48.207
Avatar Kuruk tried to warn me,
but I let it happen anyway.

43:48.208 --> 43:49.374
It's hard to explain.

43:49.375 --> 43:50.750
Okay, well,

43:52.208 --> 43:53.833
I'm here if you wanna try.

43:58.916 --> 44:00.665
When I merged with the Ocean Spirit,

44:00.666 --> 44:03.415
all I could feel
was the spirit's need for revenge.

44:03.416 --> 44:05.957
I could see the destruction
that it was causing,

44:05.958 --> 44:09.833
that I was causing,
and… I couldn't stop it.

44:11.500 --> 44:14.916
I don't want people to get hurt,
and I don't want people to die.

44:15.875 --> 44:17.500
Yeah, that must have been terrifying.

44:18.000 --> 44:21.500
I don't… wanna feel that way ever again.

44:22.125 --> 44:25.540
I know I can enter the Avatar State now,
but I'm not even gonna try it

44:25.541 --> 44:27.875
until I have full control
over all four elements.

44:30.500 --> 44:33.208
Well, we better find you
an earthbending teacher, then.

44:33.916 --> 44:35.708
Oh, and guess where we are?

44:36.291 --> 44:37.166
The Earth Kingdom.

44:37.958 --> 44:40.708
This place is probably lousy
with earthbending masters.

44:41.791 --> 44:43.125
Thank you, Sokka.

44:45.000 --> 44:49.207
If you ever wanna talk about the North,
like, what happened with Yue…

44:49.208 --> 44:51.124
[chuckles] Yeah, I… Thanks.

44:51.125 --> 44:55.041
I, um… I'm just busy with the list of, uh,

44:56.083 --> 44:59.125
uh, how to save the world
in ten easy steps.

45:00.666 --> 45:01.625
Twenty or

45:02.916 --> 45:04.416
a hundred, maybe.

45:15.833 --> 45:18.958
Hey! This is my line.
What do you think you're doing?

45:19.875 --> 45:21.082
Take it easy, kid.

45:21.083 --> 45:23.790
There's a bunch of unpicked lines
in the east field. Go pick there.

45:23.791 --> 45:25.500
And lose half an hour walking?

45:26.000 --> 45:27.166
Walk faster.

45:29.166 --> 45:32.124
There's an order to how we do things here
that can't be broken.

45:32.125 --> 45:34.333
[grunts] Who do you think you are, huh?

45:35.250 --> 45:36.708
Who do I think I am?

45:37.333 --> 45:39.499
- That's enough!
- [Zuko grunts]

45:39.500 --> 45:42.500
We get it. You're both very scary guys.

45:47.708 --> 45:50.458
Hey, Mushi, get your son in line.

45:52.375 --> 45:54.416
[string instrument strumming]

45:57.916 --> 46:01.333
[Katara] I'm glad that we got out
of that alive. I mean, no one was hurt.

46:03.375 --> 46:04.416
You did good.

46:05.666 --> 46:07.583
Hey, nice moves before with the serpent.

46:08.791 --> 46:09.708
Okay.

46:10.666 --> 46:12.166
- Thanks.
- What?

46:13.208 --> 46:15.625
Just take the compliment
and take a seat, sis.

46:19.625 --> 46:22.457
Oh! Waterbend your way out of that!

46:22.458 --> 46:25.707
- Oh! I'm sorry. Sorry.
- [Aang chuckles]

46:25.708 --> 46:27.166
- Okay!
- [Aang] Oh.

46:28.208 --> 46:29.375
[Sokka chuckles]

46:30.833 --> 46:33.333
[Sai] Yes. Yes. Good. Good, good, good.

46:35.083 --> 46:36.333
Thank you for coming.

46:38.833 --> 46:40.916
I'm sorry it took me so long
to prepare this.

46:41.666 --> 46:44.040
It's okay, Sai. Can't wait to hear
what you have to say.

46:44.041 --> 46:46.250
This is not good news.

46:46.875 --> 46:50.040
What I'm about to tell you is dangerous.
And it could swing not just the war,

46:50.041 --> 46:52.833
but the fate of our world
in the Fire Nation's favor.

46:55.750 --> 46:59.207
When Omashu fell, the Fire Nation generals
made me track celestial movements

46:59.208 --> 47:01.000
against their own historical records.

47:01.583 --> 47:05.874
It was an imperfect picture
since the smog blotted out the stars.

47:05.875 --> 47:11.083
But now, out here, I can see more clearly,
and I believe I've put it all together.

47:12.666 --> 47:13.625
Here. Look.

47:24.458 --> 47:26.666
A red dot with a tail. Do you see it?

47:27.458 --> 47:30.290
[Aang] Yeah, I see it. What is it?

47:30.291 --> 47:32.791
[Sai] That is the Great Comet.

47:33.291 --> 47:36.624
Now, in the Fire Nation,
they call that Sozin's Comet because--

47:36.625 --> 47:41.000
Because last time, Fire Lord Sozin used it
to kill every Airbender in the world.

47:41.583 --> 47:43.458
Except for me.

47:43.958 --> 47:45.958
[suspenseful music playing]

47:46.500 --> 47:49.499
Now, when the comet reaches its apsis
to our world,

47:49.500 --> 47:53.666
it will increase the power
of every Firebender 100-fold.

47:54.208 --> 47:55.666
This will be catastrophic.

47:59.958 --> 48:01.624
How long until it gets here?

48:01.625 --> 48:04.457
I'm not sure. A few months, a year, maybe.

48:04.458 --> 48:07.457
[distorted] I need the time and equipment
to make more precise observations.

48:07.458 --> 48:09.624
- [Katara] We'll help.
- [Sokka] We have to win before.

48:09.625 --> 48:12.749
- [Teo] We can use my father's inventions.
- [Katara] We need to figure out…

48:12.750 --> 48:15.332
[Sokka] Fire Nation won't see this coming.
We'll be ready…

48:15.333 --> 48:17.290
[Katara] Train Water and Earthbenders
to work…

48:17.291 --> 48:19.291
[Sokka] Yeah, and surprise him.
That's good.

48:19.958 --> 48:22.957
Change of plans. We're going to Ba Sing Se
with all the refugees.

48:22.958 --> 48:25.624
We're gonna bring Sai to the Earth King
to tell him about the comet,

48:25.625 --> 48:28.083
and the Earth King's armies
will be able to help us.

48:28.708 --> 48:30.250
Aang, what about earthbending?

48:31.083 --> 48:33.082
The search for a teacher
will have to wait.

48:33.083 --> 48:36.833
Yeah, it's still on the list.
Just lower, under catastrophic comet.

48:37.958 --> 48:39.582
[Aang] Everyone should get some rest.

48:39.583 --> 48:42.290
And tomorrow, we'll put one foot
in front of the other.

48:42.291 --> 48:45.208
We got a long way to go
before this is all over.

48:47.250 --> 48:48.833
Thank you for all your work, Sai.

48:52.208 --> 48:53.833
[somber music playing]

49:17.000 --> 49:17.999
[Sai clears throat]

49:18.000 --> 49:19.291
[music fades]

49:20.250 --> 49:23.166
You know, I used to walk
by your flower stand almost every day.

49:24.958 --> 49:25.958
I know.

49:26.791 --> 49:27.666
Oh.

49:35.041 --> 49:36.291
[Sai sighs]

49:38.416 --> 49:40.166
Our time here is so

49:41.166 --> 49:42.208
short.

49:42.958 --> 49:43.791
Hmm.

49:44.875 --> 49:47.875
I would like nothing better
than to get more acquainted with you.

49:52.750 --> 49:53.875
[woman sighs]

49:59.583 --> 50:01.583
[gentle music playing]

50:06.000 --> 50:07.125
[chuckles]

50:21.125 --> 50:22.000
Hi.

50:23.583 --> 50:24.500
Hey.

50:29.083 --> 50:31.208
Did you tell
the other Kyoshi Warriors yet?

50:32.541 --> 50:33.541
Not yet.

50:45.500 --> 50:46.416
Can I…

50:48.875 --> 50:50.875
just stay here with you for a second?

50:52.458 --> 50:53.541
Of course.

51:15.458 --> 51:17.458
[uplifting music playing]

51:54.208 --> 51:55.583
[music fades]

51:58.541 --> 51:59.375
[sighs]

52:06.375 --> 52:07.250
Katara?

52:07.750 --> 52:08.666
[Katara] Hey.

52:10.666 --> 52:11.583
What's up?

52:23.791 --> 52:24.875
Nothing.

52:26.958 --> 52:27.958
Good night.

52:30.208 --> 52:31.250
Good night.

52:33.416 --> 52:35.416
[gentle music playing]

52:40.333 --> 52:41.708
[music fades]

52:42.875 --> 52:46.582
[Mai] If your father wants him back,
does that mean his banishment is lifted?

52:46.583 --> 52:48.707
But he's not coming home
in a good way, right?

52:48.708 --> 52:51.250
It's more like, "Come home,
the Fire Lord is mad at you."

52:51.833 --> 52:54.915
Oh, or disappointed. That's worse.

52:54.916 --> 52:55.915
Unknown.

52:55.916 --> 52:58.541
As usual,
my father's intentions are a mystery.

52:59.041 --> 53:02.749
Well, New Ozai's fallen apart
since he left my father in charge.

53:02.750 --> 53:04.915
If I never see
another crumbling boulder again,

53:04.916 --> 53:06.541
I might almost be happy.

53:08.291 --> 53:10.374
I heard she rescued you from the circus.

53:10.375 --> 53:11.499
Me?

53:11.500 --> 53:14.916
Oh, yeah. I'm so rescued.

53:17.083 --> 53:19.082
There's only so far
you can go into the forest

53:19.083 --> 53:21.374
before you start
to come out of the forest.

53:21.375 --> 53:23.625
- Ooh, philosophy.
- What?

53:25.500 --> 53:26.416
Mai.

53:28.166 --> 53:30.582
I know you used to have a crush on Zuko.
Tell me.

53:30.583 --> 53:32.625
How deep do your feelings run?

53:33.208 --> 53:35.208
You mean if you were both drowning,
who would I save?

53:36.750 --> 53:38.541
Zuko, obviously.

53:39.083 --> 53:41.958
I've known you long enough
to know you don't need saving.

53:43.375 --> 53:44.458
Interesting.

53:45.208 --> 53:47.750
That sounds like logic and not feelings.

53:49.166 --> 53:51.999
Ty Lee, I want you to kill Mei.

53:52.000 --> 53:52.915
[Ty Lee] What?

53:52.916 --> 53:54.790
- [Azula] Mai, I want you to kill Ty Lee.
- What?

53:54.791 --> 53:56.540
I'm gonna count down from ten.

53:56.541 --> 53:57.915
- Azula, what?
- You're joking.

53:57.916 --> 54:01.041
By the time I reach one,
I expect one of you to be dead.

54:04.416 --> 54:06.832
Or I'll turn you both
into smoldering heaps of ash.

54:06.833 --> 54:08.791
[ominous music playing]

54:10.500 --> 54:12.707
- Ten.
- Azula, I will really kill her.

54:12.708 --> 54:14.207
No, don't really kill me.

54:14.208 --> 54:16.208
- Nine.
- Azula, stop.

54:16.958 --> 54:17.791
Eight.

54:20.833 --> 54:22.041
Seven.

54:23.958 --> 54:25.083
[grunts]

54:26.875 --> 54:27.790
Why?

54:27.791 --> 54:29.125
Six.

54:30.083 --> 54:31.083
[grunts]

54:32.500 --> 54:33.458
[grunts]

54:34.708 --> 54:35.750
[grunts]

54:38.958 --> 54:40.165
[Azula] Five.

54:40.166 --> 54:42.166
[grunting]

54:43.666 --> 54:44.790
[Azula] Four.

54:44.791 --> 54:46.833
[grunting]

54:47.666 --> 54:48.915
We don't have to do this.

54:48.916 --> 54:50.583
- You know that we do.
- Three.

54:52.333 --> 54:53.291
Fine.

54:54.166 --> 54:56.125
[grunting]

54:57.125 --> 54:58.291
Two.

55:00.416 --> 55:01.332
Enough.

55:01.333 --> 55:02.749
[both panting]

55:02.750 --> 55:03.750
[Azula slow clapping]

55:08.291 --> 55:10.832
Thank you. I knew I could trust you both.

55:10.833 --> 55:12.958
But I needed to know
you could go all the way for me.

55:14.125 --> 55:15.957
[Ty Lee] Why would you need that?

55:15.958 --> 55:17.999
[Azula] Because
I have a plan to find Zuko.

55:18.000 --> 55:20.791
A way to bring Zuko to us, in fact.

55:24.791 --> 55:26.750
We're going after the Avatar.

55:28.291 --> 55:30.291
[fire crackling]

55:44.666 --> 55:45.791
[Iroh clears throat]

55:56.375 --> 55:57.791
You haven't been eating.

56:02.833 --> 56:03.666
Hmm.

56:07.541 --> 56:10.166
We were forced to do this
because we're in hiding.

56:10.666 --> 56:12.958
Fugitives from our own country.

56:13.875 --> 56:15.458
I know the work is hard,

56:15.958 --> 56:21.415
but there is a simple joy to be had
in the sweat, the creaking of bones,

56:21.416 --> 56:24.582
the slow progress
towards something that matters.

56:24.583 --> 56:27.333
Living the austere life, hmm?

56:31.833 --> 56:34.166
I've accepted our circumstances.

56:34.916 --> 56:39.916
And I've saved most of my earnings
to open a small tea stall in a small town.

56:40.916 --> 56:43.125
I could teach you to brew the tea,

56:43.958 --> 56:47.208
and you might even learn
to enjoy the craft.

56:48.166 --> 56:52.541
The right cup of tea at the right moment
can change your entire life, hmm?

56:53.125 --> 56:55.625
It's how I got Zarina
to fall in love with me.

56:57.416 --> 56:59.291
Maybe your life can change.

56:59.791 --> 57:01.083
Out here

57:02.208 --> 57:06.208
in a quiet part of the world,
away from the troubles of the past.

57:11.666 --> 57:13.791
We've been given a gift, Zuko.

57:14.916 --> 57:16.916
A rare and precious one.

57:17.500 --> 57:19.333
The chance to start over.

57:21.250 --> 57:23.166
Don't squander it.

57:30.750 --> 57:31.833
[Zuko sighs]

57:45.500 --> 57:46.958
I'm not your son.

57:51.750 --> 57:52.916
I know that.

57:58.833 --> 58:00.833
You know what I can't stand?

58:02.083 --> 58:05.958
Your smiles, the little jokes,

58:07.458 --> 58:10.916
the affection you give
to these sod-busting peons

58:12.291 --> 58:14.165
who would despise you

58:14.166 --> 58:16.958
if they had any inkling
of who you really are.

58:21.208 --> 58:22.750
Living is a choice.

58:23.500 --> 58:25.125
I choose to be happy.

58:25.625 --> 58:27.500
To try and spread joy.

58:30.500 --> 58:32.166
[Zuko sighs]

58:39.541 --> 58:41.375
You don't deserve joy.

58:46.958 --> 58:48.791
All of this is your fault.

58:50.708 --> 58:52.875
Everything that has happened to me.

58:53.375 --> 58:54.416
My fault?

58:55.333 --> 58:58.000
- I didn't banish you.
- You broke!

59:01.041 --> 59:03.875
You were meant to be Fire Lord,
not my father.

59:05.958 --> 59:08.875
If you hadn't failed in the siege
and retreated…

59:09.708 --> 59:13.625
If you hadn't stood by and done nothing
when my father usurped you…

59:14.208 --> 59:18.000
If you had stood up to him
and fought for what was yours…

59:21.916 --> 59:25.166
then I would've never been
in that war council.

59:25.666 --> 59:27.166
In that Agni Kai.

59:30.166 --> 59:31.500
On that ship.

59:35.041 --> 59:36.916
None of this would've happened.

59:38.250 --> 59:40.041
It's your fault.

59:41.125 --> 59:42.249
Because of your weakness.

59:42.250 --> 59:44.791
Because your moment was there,
and you didn't fight!

59:50.333 --> 59:52.125
Lu Ten died.

01:00:09.041 --> 01:00:10.875
And what would he think of you

01:00:12.041 --> 01:00:13.666
if he could see you now?

01:00:17.041 --> 01:00:19.041
[somber music playing]

01:00:31.458 --> 01:00:33.541
I'm gonna go find the Avatar.

01:00:35.041 --> 01:00:36.750
And then I'm gonna go home.

01:00:44.375 --> 01:00:45.708
Goodbye, Uncle.

01:01:04.500 --> 01:01:06.416
[dramatic, adventurous music playing]
